## Intuition
The key idea is to check every pair of adjacent elements. An array is sorted in non-decreasing order if each element is less than or equal to the element immediately after it. So, if we ever find arr[i] > arr[i+1], the array is not sorted.

## Approach

1. Traverse the array from the first element up to the second-last element.
1. For each index i, compare arr[i] with arr[i+1].
1. If arr[i] > arr[i+1], return false immediately because the array is not sorted.
1. If no such pair is found after checking the entire array, return true.
1. The approach also handles edge cases naturally:
1. An empty or single-element array is considered sorted because there are no adjacent elements out of order.
1. Duplicate elements are allowed because the condition only fails when arr[i] > arr[i+1].

